@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam roundcorner 14
skinparam ArrowColor #64748B
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.8
skinparam titleFontSize 19
skinparam titleFontStyle bold
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor #0F172A
  FontStyle bold
  FontSize 11
  BorderColor #334155
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #94A3B8
  FontColor #0F172A
}

title Business Continuity — What Happens When the Site in Charge Dies

rectangle "<b>STEADY STATE</b>\nchanges recorded and acknowledged\nenquiries answered from every site" as N1 #DCFCE7
rectangle "<b>READING GROWS</b>\nspare capacity is added,\nno application is changed" as N2 #DCFCE7
rectangle "<b>WRITING GROWS</b>\nbusiness is divided into parts,\neach with its own leader" as N3 #DBEAFE

rectangle "<b>THE SITE IN CHARGE DIES</b>\nsuddenly, without warning" as F1 #FECACA
rectangle "<b>ENQUIRIES ARE NOT INTERRUPTED</b>\nthe live mirror carries straight on" as F2 #FEF3C7
rectangle "<b>CHANGES ARE HELD, NOT LOST</b>\nnothing reaches a half-dead site" as F3 #FEF3C7
rectangle "<b>FAILURE DETECTED</b>\nwithin seconds, no human involved" as F4 #FEF3C7
rectangle "<b>FAILED SITE STOOD DOWN</b>\nso it can never disagree" as F5 #FEF3C7

rectangle "<b>THE MIRROR IS PROMOTED</b>\nit becomes the site in charge" as R1 #BBF7D0
rectangle "<b>WRITING RESUMES</b>\nsame unchanged connection" as R2 #86EFAC

rectangle "failed site resynchronised\nin the background" as B1 #DBEAFE
rectangle "rejoins as a follower\nunder operator control" as B2 #DBEAFE
rectangle "<b>FULL SERVICE RESTORED</b>\nready to do it all again" as B3 #E0F2FE

N1 -down-> N2
N2 -down-> N3
N3 -down-> F1
F1 -down-> F2
F2 -down-> F3
F3 -down-> F4
F4 -down-> F5
F5 -down-> R1
R1 -down-> R2
R2 -down-> B1
B1 -down-> B2
B2 -down-> B3

note right of R2
  **Measured recovery: 5 to 10 seconds.**

  The recovery is automatic, and it is
  rehearsed by a repeatable test.
  It is not a hope - it is demonstrated.

  **What this design costs us:** because the
  mirror is made a moment apart, the very last
  few changes could be lost at the instant of
  failure.

  A regulated institution would close that gap.
  This design deliberately does not yet,
  and says so rather than hiding it.
end note

legend bottom
  |= Phase | What the customer experiences |
  | <#DCFCE7> | Running normally |
  | <#FECACA> | The failure itself |
  | <#FEF3C7> | The automatic response |
  | <#BBF7D0> | Business resumes |
  | <#DBEAFE> | Putting things right |
endlegend

@enduml